Why 5.6.0: the cmsis-device-g0 README defers to the STM32CubeG0 release notes for
the CMSIS Core version. STM32CubeG0 v1.6.3, the release that ships
"STM32G0xx CMSIS V1.4.5", lists "CMSIS V5.6.0_cm0".

Files, copied unmodified from upstream CMSIS/Core/Include/:
  core_cm0plus.h      included by stm32g031xx.h
  cmsis_version.h     included by core_cm0plus.h
  cmsis_compiler.h    included by core_cm0plus.h
  cmsis_gcc.h         what cmsis_compiler.h includes for GCC (and upstream clang)
  mpu_armv7.h         included by core_cm0plus.h, since the G031 sets __MPU_PRESENT 1

Not copied: the other compilers' headers that cmsis_compiler.h can pick
(cmsis_armcc.h, cmsis_armclang*.h, cmsis_iccarm.h). Only arm-none-eabi-gcc is used.
